# Semgrep SAST (server.yml job `sast`). Only vendored or generated code belongs here — never
# a path just because it has findings (fix it, or `nosemgrep: rule-id -- reason` inline).
# On a pull_request CI reads this file from the BASE commit, so an edit takes effect once merged.
# Root only: CI fails on a .semgrepignore in any subdirectory (Semgrep would honour it).
# A .semgrepignore replaces Semgrep's built-in default ignores, so node_modules is listed too.
node_modules/
server/dist/
# Vendored web assets (bundled third-party builds, pinned in VERSION/WEB_DB_ASSET_VERSIONS files).
frontend/web/zxing/
frontend/web/drift_worker.js
frontend/web/sqlite3*
# Generated Dart (Drift codegen etc.).
*.g.dart
